{"id": "EUVD-2026-93209", "enisaUuid": "ce275313-f51b-3f81-90bd-1e77ce4871ef", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfutex: Also allocate private hash on vfork()\n\nAs Jann demonstrated, it is entirely feasible to access the mm through vfork().\nTherefore we need to allocate a private hash on vfork() as well as any other\nCLONE_VM user.\n\nSpecifically, it must be avoided to have (private) futex waiters before\nallocating the private hash.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:52", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5468a4855b63b30156a79e5248e01bf1a2c18dd7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eecbafa8cabbc4d1482f6a5e2acc25a8f934681b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b61b6f95d6722ddbbbd09e689fa41b55fd36f9a5"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fwjp-32v8-7pp8", "CVE-2026-98281"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "13a9d53a-9c66-3f3c-8d99-7f882db62a43", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1e33a887-31b2-3806-b292-68af0333d300", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "4ee57518-aa37-3707-b2f4-f5cf6df61344", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "974ac49a9a068b0591a59f65c63eb06579a13091"}, {"id": "4f6c7d45-522b-384c-9b3a-e39ebc109aab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1"}, {"id": "6498e412-dab7-3692-b50d-dc7d79e61e98", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1dcd36420af2da5bd59306dba9caf78e3d248b1d <5468a4855b63b30156a79e5248e01bf1a2c18dd7"}, {"id": "67d15384-ed12-3a86-9ef2-890888efc3a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "874ba14d-06af-3b33